Validation by deletion of the committed-matrix proof, 2026-09-16

Toy block (regular layout), one claim whose value is off by one; the matrix verifier run against:
- an honest proof of the wrong value ("main");
- a forged proof whose last prefix-table count is adjusted so the main sumcheck closes ("count");
- a forged proof that also adjusts one address bit so the count sumcheck closes ("opening").
The forging prover is `matrix::prove_forged` (feature `forgery`); the same forgeries are asserted in
`crates/lift/tests/matrix.rs` (`toy_forged_proofs_are_refused_by_the_check_they_target`).

== intact
DELETION main: Err(Main)
DELETION count: Err(Count)
DELETION opening: Err(Opening)
== main check deleted (the comparison of the main sumcheck's final claim with the counts)
DELETION main: Ok(())
== count check deleted (the comparison of the count sumcheck's final claim with the address bits)
DELETION count: Ok(())
== opening deleted (the Ligerito opening of the committed entry list)
DELETION opening: Ok(())

So each of the three checks is what refuses a forgery that passes the checks before it. Every edit
was reverted from a saved copy; the tree at commit time is the unmodified one.
